 "section_summary": "This section contains extensive bibliographies of American children's literature and adult books on educational theory, school curricula, and American life and history selected for shipment to Japan following World War II. It concludes with correspondence between National Education Association Executive Secretary Willard E. Givens and Assistant Secretary of State William Benton regarding the implementation of book donation initiatives proposed by the United States Education Mission to Japan. Benton affirms State Department support for providing these educational materials to Japanese teachers, children, and education committee members to assist in democratic reorientation.",
